# A client calls an API behind a rate limiter, three times. Each time the limiter checks a token bucket
# in Redis. Branch: with tokens left the request is forwarded and answered; when the bucket is empty the
# limiter rejects it with 429 and the client backs off before the next attempt.
title Rate-limited API calls
speed 0.9
client[Client]{shape: circle} -> limiter[Rate Limiter]{shape: round} : GET /orders
loop 3
  limiter -> bucket[Token Bucket]{shape: db, color: #f59e0b} : take token
  branch token available
    bucket --> limiter : ok
    limiter -> api[Orders API] : forward
    api --> client : 200 @0.6s
  else bucket empty
    bucket -x limiter : empty
    limiter -x client : 429 Too Many Requests
    wait 0.8
  end
  client -> limiter : next request
end
